// Dedicated wire-conformance fixture for the protobuf-es TS server.
//
// This is the ENCODE-side mirror of the client fixture
// (internal/tsclientgen/testdata/es/conformance.proto). The client proof asks
// "does fromJson decode what the Go server sent?"; this one asks the opposite
// and equally load-bearing question: "does toJson(create(...)) emit what a Go
// server would have emitted?" — because an es-mode server is what produces the
// body every sebuf client, Go or TS, has to read.
//
// The fields below are chosen so a single encode exercises every place where
// protobuf-es's canonical JSON output could drift from Go's protojson:
//   - zero-valued scalars/bools/lists must be OMITTED, not emitted as "" / 0 /
//     false / [];
//   - 64-bit ints must leave as JSON STRINGS, preserving values past 2^53;
//   - a partially-populated nested message must emit only its set fields;
//   - maps must emit as JSON objects;
//   - enums must emit as their NAME string, and the zero value must be omitted.
//
// It is intentionally standalone: no service, no sebuf/http imports, so
// protoc-gen-es emits a clean _pb module that only depends on
// @bufbuild/protobuf. Generate the JS the conformance test imports with:
//
//   protoc \
//     --plugin=protoc-gen-es=.scratch/es-spike/node_modules/.bin/protoc-gen-es \
//     --es_out=internal/tsservergen/testdata/es \
//     --es_opt=target=js,import_extension=js \
//     --proto_path=internal/tsservergen/testdata/es \
//     conformance.proto

